# C16 Crunch

Read **`SPEC.md`** before changing display, input, or the level generator.

## Never

- Bank out the kernal (jiffy and the IRQ entry stay available)
- Point the TED charset at `$2000` before that RAM is filled
- Redefine `$01`–`$1A` (A–Z)
- Store 0 into `lfsr` or `rng16`
- Collide using screen RAM (use `playfield[]`)
- Poke screen or color RAM outside VBlank
- Use a single monster spawn cell; monsters are placed by the generator

## Always

- Stock screen `$0C00`, color `$0800`, charset RAM `$2000`
- Stub at `$1001`
- Playfield 32×16 at column 4, row 4
- Loop: input → player/monsters/bullet → TED raster → blit
- Update `SPEC.md` when a behavior change is locked
